Used to represent negative numbers in most languages.

Can represent (where 2^n-1 = X) -(X) to (X - 1)

To convert just flip the bits and add 1. Or in all honesty, you take 2^n and subtract the number from it.

For e.g., in a 8bit system, 0xff is -1 because its 2^8 = 256 => 256 - 1, 254 is -2 and so forth.

Useful because you can do addition/subtraction/mutiplication with positive and negative numbers (in the 2s complement form) using regular arithmentic operators and the overflow/carry bits.
